{
  "description": "Rating ladder and fail-closed filter (docs/rules-format.md, 'Maximum rating and the rating ladder'). normalise: trim U+0020 from both ends, upper-case ASCII a-z only, look the result up on the ladder (Approved is the ladder name Approved, rank 0, the same tier as G); otherwise a TV-PG-, TV-14- or TV-MA- rating followed by one descriptor group counts as its base rating, where the group is a non-empty run of D, L, S, V in that order, each at most once (TV-MA: L, S, V only). 'normalised' is the ladder spelling or null; 'rank' is 0 to 7 or null (no rank: blocked under any ceiling). Whitespace, control and format characters are written as JSON escapes (such as \\u00a0 for a no-break space) so that they can be seen; this file is all ASCII.",
  "source": "Expected values come from an independent Python reference that reads Jellyfin v12.1 Emby.Server.Implementations/Localization/Ratings/us.json: every Jellyfin US string appears in 'normalise' with the tier Jellyfin gives it, and Jellyfin's score maps to our rank (0->0, 7->1, 10->2, 13->3, 14->4, 17 sub-score 0->5, 17 sub-score 1->6, 18->7). Strings Jellyfin resolves by other means (country prefixes, 'Rated ', plain numbers, '/' lists) have no rank here on purpose: the filter fails closed. 'inheritance' comes from a second independent Python reference written from the amended rule 4 in docs/rules-format.md alone: an episode is eligible under a ceiling only if (a) its effective rating passes (its own, or the series' when its own is none or the empty string) and (b) the series' rating passes whenever the series has one (anything but none or the empty string); a series not in the snapshot blocks; a loose episode uses (a) with its own rating; no ceiling admits everything.",
