  "inheritanceNote": "Each row is an episode: 'own' is its own rating, 'seriesState' says what is known of its series, and 'maxRating' is the ceiling (null for none). 'series' is read only when seriesState is 'known'; there it is the series' rating, null or the empty string meaning the series has none. Under a ceiling an episode is eligible only if (a) its effective rating passes, which is its own rating, or the series' when its own is absent (null or the empty string) and seriesState is 'known', and (b) when seriesState is 'known' and the series has a rating (anything but null or the empty string), that rating passes too; NR, Unrated and a blank ' ' have no rank, so a series rated so blocks its episodes. seriesState 'unknown' (the series is not in the snapshot) is blocked under any ceiling. seriesState 'none' (a loose episode with no series) is checked under (a) alone, with its own rating. Any other own rating, including NR or a blank ' ', is used as it is. With maxRating null, every item is eligible. Why (b): an episode's own rating is often a copy of its series' rating, and whether that copy follows a re-rating of the series is not verified; (b) keeps the ceiling safe whatever the copy says.",
